A||||2||deceler8||Looking for styled steel wheels to fit...||||5
Z||000000||deceler8||10-05-1999||11:26 AM||||I have a base 1986 2m4 with steel wheels/wheelcovers and I'd like to change them out for something better looking.<P>I really don't want aluminum wheels and am wondering if there are any styled steel wheels that will fit the Fiero. I don't recall ever seeing any OE styled steel wheels on any Fiero. I'd like steel since they're less prone to leaks and nobody steals them, especially factory wheels. Not looking for wide wheels either...stock width (5.5" or 6").<P>Seems I saw that Dodge Shadow wheels will fit...any others that might work to anyone's knowledge ?<P>Thanks again to all the loyal Fiero folk for providing assistance.||||reg||5
Z||000001||HarryG||10-05-1999||12:20 PM||||Check at your local Public Library for the Hollander Wheel Interchange Manual; this has descriptions and pictures.  If they don't have it, ask if they can get it on Interlibrary Loan.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||10-05-1999||12:58 PM||||For 5 or 6 years now, Sunbirds, Cavaliers and Grand Ams have been equipped with 15x6 steel wheels that will fit Fieros.  They're flat black, but you could always jazz them up with nice wheel covers or beauty rings.<P>You could probably pick up a set for $50 or so at a junkyard.  I was thinking of buying a set and mounting winter tires on them for the snow season.||||reg||1
